From: Flexbuild <flexbuild@nxp.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gst: add gst_state_get_name alias for GStreamer 1.28 ABI compat

GStreamer 1.28 added gst_state_get_name() as a shorter alias for the
long-standing gst_element_state_get_name(). Debian 13's libgstplay-1.0
is built against GStreamer 1.28 and requires this symbol at runtime.
Add the alias to the 1.26 NXP fork so that Debian gst-plugins-bad 1.28
libraries resolve the symbol against this GStreamer 1.26 core.

Signed-off-by: Flexbuild <flexbuild@nxp.com>
---
 gst/gstutils.c | 7 +++++++
 gst/gstutils.h | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gst/gstutils.c b/gst/gstutils.c
--- a/gst/gstutils.c
+++ b/gst/gstutils.c
@@ -1300,7 +1300,14 @@
       return g_strdup_printf ("UNKNOWN!(%d)", state);
   }
 }

+/* Alias added for GStreamer 1.28 API compatibility */
+const gchar *
+gst_state_get_name (GstState state)
+{
+  return gst_element_state_get_name (state);
+}
+
 /**
  * gst_element_state_change_return_get_name:
  * @state_ret: a #GstStateChangeReturn to get the name of.
diff --git a/gst/gstutils.h b/gst/gstutils.h
--- a/gst/gstutils.h
+++ b/gst/gstutils.h
@@ -992,6 +992,9 @@
 GST_API
 const gchar*            gst_element_state_get_name      (GstState state);

+GST_API
+const gchar*            gst_state_get_name              (GstState state);
+
 GST_API
 const gchar *           gst_element_state_change_return_get_name (GstStateChangeReturn state_ret);

